# Dependencies and build output
node_modules/

# THE READER MODEL AND ITS RUNTIME (src/embedder.js). Both are staged by
# `npm run models` — the weights downloaded once from the Hugging Face hub,
# the browser build of transformers.js copied out of node_modules — and are
# 24 MB and 22 MB of binary that would sit in history forever. Named lang/
# rather than models/ on purpose: models/ was the old .glb scratch area
# (see below), and a folder the game depends on must never share a name
# with one somebody is told it is safe to empty. Without either the game
# still runs; it reads typed messages with the phrase matcher instead.
lang/
vendor/
dist/
build/icon.png

# ref/ is deliberately NOT ignored. tools/glb2hulls.js consumes the .glb
# models, so without them the ship meshes cannot be regenerated and the
# repo is not self-contained. They are also the only copy that exists.

# Scratch
_basetest/
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# OS and editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
  
# Generated-file backups. Git is the backup now.  
*.prev  

# Scratch test output.
_test_output.txt

# Claude's working area: probe output, suite logs, patches and backups
# from every session. Scratch by design; the repo is the record.
Claude outputs/

# THE WORKING COPIES OF PACKED FILES (tools/pack.cjs, 2026-10-30). What
# git tracks is the .gz beside each of these; the plain file is only there
# so Blender and the tools can open it. `npm run unpack` writes them out,
# `npm run pack` stores your changes, and `npm test` fails while a working
# copy differs from what is stored.
ref/**/*.glb
new models/**/*.glb
src/ports/*.js

# The models/ staging area. Almost every .glb in it duplicated ref/glb/ —
# the copy tools/glb2hulls.js actually consumes — with a third copy under
# "models/Manifest Models/uploads/". Tracking it would have written the same
# ~60 MB into history three times and git never lets those bytes go again.
#
# THE SENTENCE THAT USED TO BE HERE WAS WRONG, and the error was nearly
# expensive. It said the station-design sketch was "the one thing in there
# that was not a duplicate". It was not: buried under Manifest Models/
# uploads/ were twenty-four PORT models — the cylinder station, city ports,
# runway and pad sites, comets, detail kits — that existed in no other
# place, fifteen of them planetside ports that station-lab cannot rebuild
# because the lab exports orbital patterns only. A request to delete the old
# models would have taken all of it, on the strength of this comment.
#
# They are now tracked under ref/ports/ and ref/port-art/ (see that folder's
# README), and models/ itself is gone. The rule stands for anything staged
# here in future: this directory is scratch, so check it for originals with
# tools/rescue-port-art.ps1 before emptying it, and do not trust a comment
# that says there is nothing here.
models/

# Synthetic port models. Unlike ref/, these are GENERATED — recreate them
# with `node tools/make-port-fixture.js` — and they are binary, which is
# the one thing a diff cannot help with. Real port art belongs in
# ref/ports/ and is tracked like every other model.
test/fixtures/

# tools/pack.cjs's record of what each working copy was when last in sync.
.pack-state.json
